(a) The city planning and zoning commission shall be composed of seven members. Each commissioner from each commission district will appoint one member, totaling six members, and the mayor will appoint one additional member, to comprise the seven-member board. The appointed members shall be registered voters of the city. No member of the planning and zoning commission shall be persons who hold elected public office in the city or Wayne County, Georgia. Appointments to the planning and zoning commission shall be for overlapping terms of three years with terms expiring on December 31. The mayor's initial appointment to this planning and zoning commission may occur following the passage of this section and will be effective for the remaining term and duration of existing appointments already made by the board of commissioners. Thereafter, the regular initial appointments to the planning and zoning commission which first occur after the passage of this section (and including the mayor's regular initial appointment that will also be available at that time) shall be made so that the terms of said members shall be staggered. In order to establish staggered terms, the initial terms of two members shall be one year, and the initial terms of another two members will be two years, and the initial terms of another three members will be for three years. The members serving the one-year terms, the two-year terms, and the three-year terms shall be determined by agreement of the board of commissioners of the city and the mayor or by lot in the absence of such agreement. If at the end of any term of office of a member, a successor thereto shall not have been appointed, then the member whose term of office shall have expired shall continue to hold office until his or her successor shall be so appointed. Any vacancy in the planning and zoning commission shall be filled by appointment by the commissioner or mayor who made the original appointment to the planning and zoning commission that is then vacant. In the event of the vacancy of the commissioner or mayor who made such original appointment to the planning and zoning commission, any such vacancy in the planning and zoning commission shall be appointed by an affirmative majority vote of the remaining commissioners and the mayor. Members of the planning and zoning commission can serve successive terms without limit. The members of the planning and zoning commission shall receive no compensation for their services, and shall at all times maintain a current mailing address and telephone number on file with the city.
(b) The board of commissioners of the city shall be authorized to remove any member for cause after written notice and public hearing. Any one or more of the following shall constitute a reason for removing a member "for cause":
(1) Participating as a member of the planning and zoning commission at any regular or called meeting of the planning and zoning commission under the influence of intoxicants, alcohol, or unprescribed or illegal drugs or using, possessing or selling the same in violation of the laws of the State of Georgia;
(2) Charge and accusation for a misdemeanor which would adversely affect performance of his or her duties as a member of the planning and zoning commission;
(3) Conduct unbecoming of a member of the planning and zoning commission, including, but not limited to, demeaning conduct or use of profanity or vulgar language during any open public meeting of the planning and zoning commission;
(4) Indictment of a felony;
(5) Unauthorized use of city property, city telephones or other city communication equipment;
(6) Filing false expense reports;
(7) Three consecutive absences from planning and zoning commission meetings without obtaining prior approval of a majority of the remaining members of the planning and zoning commission; or
(8) Repeated and continued discourteous treatment of members of the public during planning and zoning commission meetings after being admonished concerning such conduct by the board of commissioners of the city.
Charges for "removable for cause" may be made by any city commissioner, any member of the planning and zoning commission or by any citizen of the city. Any such charges must be made in writing, dated, signed and delivered to the board of commissioners of the city. A copy of any such charge must be mailed to the member of the planning and zoning commission against whom the charge is directed. Upon receipt of any such charge the board of commissioners of the city will then set a date and time for a public hearing. The city manager will notify both the party making the charge and the member of the planning and zoning commission against whom the charges are directed of the date, time and place of the public hearing. The member of the planning and zoning commission against whom charges are made shall have at least two weeks' notice prior to the date set for the public hearing to prepare for the public hearing. In the event, after the public hearing, the board of commissioners of the city, by majority vote, removes the member of the planning and zoning commission, the board of commissioners of the city will then proceed to fill the vacancy for the unexpired term pursuant to the foregoing provisions of this section.
(Code 1976, § 23-16; Ord. of 12-17-2002, § 23-16; Ord. No. 2017-004, § 1, 2-7-2017; Ord. of 3-7-2017(1), § 1)
Editor's note— Ord. No. 2017-004, § 1, adopted Feb. 7, 2017, changed the title of § 70-31 from "Created; membership" to read as herein set out.

